{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"Given that both \\(i - 3\\) and \\(b\\) are roots of the polynomial \\(ax^3 + 9x^2 + ax - 30\\), and knowing that the coefficients are real, the complex roots must occur in conjugate pairs. Therefore, \\(-i - 3\\) is also a root of the polynomial.\n\nThe polynomial can be expressed as:\n\\[a(x - (i - 3))(x - (-i - 3))(x - b) = a(x - i + 3)(x + i + 3)(x - b)\\]\n\nFirst, we simplify the product of the complex conjugate factors:\n\\[(x - i + 3)(x + i + 3) = (x + 3 - i)(x + 3 + i) = (x + 3)^2 - i^2 = (x + 3)^2 + 1 = x^2 + 6x + 9 + 1 = x^2 + 6x + 10\\]\n\nSo the polynomial becomes:\n\\[a(x^2 + 6x + 10)(x - b)\\]\n\nExpanding this product, we get:\n\\[a(x^3 - bx^2 + 6x^2 - 6bx + 10x - 10b) = a(x^3 + (6 - b)x^2 + (10 - 6b)x - 10b)\\]\n\n","prefix_end":711,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[22043,429,2176,17767,72,481,220,18,57758,323,17767,65,57758,525,19703,315,279,47311,17767,706,61,18,488,220,24,87,61,17,488,3859,481,220,18,15,59,701,323,14063,429,279,36829,525,1931,11,279,6351,19703,1969,12170,304,63280,349,13530,13,15277,11,1124,4080,72,481,220,18,57758,374,1083,264,3704,315,279,47311,382,785,47311,646,387,13302,438,510,78045,64,2075,481,320,72,481,220,18,28154,87,481,10293,72,481,220,18,28154,87,481,293,8,284,264,2075,481,600,488,220,18,2376,87,488,600,488,220,18,2376,87,481,293,10699,2533,5338,11,582,39721,279,1985,315,279,6351,63280,349,9363,510,59,9697,87,481,600,488,220,18,2376,87,488,600,488,220,18,8,284,320,87,488,220,18,481,600,2376,87,488,220,18,488,600,8,284,320,87,488,220,18,29776,17,481,600,61,17,284,320,87,488,220,18,29776,17,488,220,16,284,856,61,17,488,220,21,87,488,220,24,488,220,16,284,856,61,17,488,220,21,87,488,220,16,15,59,2533,4416,279,47311,9044,510,78045,64,2075,61,17,488,220,21,87,488,220,16,15,2376,87,481,293,10699,2533,8033,25591,419,1985,11,582,633,510,78045,64,2075,61,18,481,44241,61,1